About CloudWalk: We are not just another fintech unicorn. We are a pack of dreamers, makers, and tech enthusiasts building the future of payments. With millions of customers and a hunger for innovation, we're now expanding our neural network - literally and metaphorically. What You'll Be Doing:
Support privacy and security incident response involving personal data, including triage, containment, root cause analysis and remediation tracking;
Assess incident scope and severity by identifying affected systems, data categories, impacted data subjects, logs, APIs, databases and exposure vectors;
Review privacy, security and data governance documentation, including incident response playbooks, technical procedures and access control materials;

Strong communication skills to translate technical findings, such as cloud misconfigurations, access control gaps or log exposure, into privacy, regulatory and business risks;
Ability to support incident handling activities, including impact assessment, evidence gathering, containment follow-up and remediation tracking;
Ability to work with Security, Engineering, Product, Legal and Compliance teams on privacy and security-related topics;

Previous experience in Privacy, Data Protection, Information Security, GRC, SecOps or Incident Response;
Hands-on experience with incidents involving cloud environments, logs, credentials or access control failures;
Technical familiarity with cloud infrastructure, monitoring, logging, encryption and identity/access management;
Join us at CloudWalk, where we’re not just engineering solutions; we’re building a smarter, AI-driven future for payments—together. By applying for this position, your data will be processed as per CloudWalk's Privacy Policy that you can read here in Portuguese and here in English.

